"""
    variation(; offset, size, sourcetype, consequencetype, wildtype, alternativesequence, location, accession, disease, omim, evidence, taxid, dbtype, dbid, accept = nothing, parse = true, send = true)

Search natural variants in UniProt

Among the available response content types, PEFF format (PSI Extended FASTA Format from the Human Proteome Organisation - Proteomics Standards Initiative, HUPO-PSI) is provided with only variants reported in the output.

`GET /variation` (operationId `search_14`, tag `variation`)

# Query parameters
- `offset::Integer` (spec: integer/int32; default `0`): Off set, page starting point, with default value 0
- `size::Integer` (spec: integer/int32; default `100`): Page size with default value 100. When page size is -1, it returns all records and offset will be ignored
- `sourcetype::ListParam` (spec: string; pattern `^(uniprot|large scale study|mixed|clinvar|nci-tcga|cosmic curated|ensembl|gnomad|topmed|exac)(,(uniprot|large scale study|mixed|clinvar|nci-tcga|cosmic curated|ensembl|gnomad|topmed|exac))*\$`): Filter by the sourceType for variants: uniprot, large scale study, mixed, clinvar, nci-tcga, cosmic curated, ensembl, gnomad, topmed and exac. Comma separated values accepted up to 2.
- `consequencetype::ListParam` (spec: string; pattern `^(missense|stop\\sgained|stop\\slost)(,(missense|stop\\sgained|stop\\slost))*\$`): Filter by consequenceType for variants: missense, stop gained or stop lost. Comma separated values accepted up to 2.
- `wildtype::ListParam` (spec: string; pattern `^[A-Za-z\\-]{1,20}(,[A-Za-z\\-]{1,20})*\$`): Search by specific wildType amino acid. Options: Any single letter amino acid and * for stop codon. Comma separated values accepted up to 20.
- `alternativesequence::ListParam` (spec: string; pattern `^[A-Za-z\\-]{1,20}(,[A-Za-z\\-]{1,20})*\$`): Filter by the alternativeSequence amino acid. Any single letter amino acid and * for stopcodon and - for deletions. Comma separated values accepted up to 20.
- `location::AbstractString` (spec: string): Filter by the amino acid range position in the sequence(s). Any valid amino acid range position within the length of the protein sequence such as 10-60 (start position to end position)
- `accession::AbstractString` (spec: string): UniProt accession(s). Comma separated values accepted up to 100.
- `disease::AbstractString` (spec: string): Search by disease name/ acronym for associated variants , e.g. alzheimer disease 1 or AD1. Partial names allowed.
- `omim::IntListParam` (spec: string; pattern `^[0-9]+(,[0-9]+)*\$`): Search by MIM ID, e.g. 104300. Comma separated values accepted up to 20.
- `evidence::IntListParam` (spec: string; pattern `^[0-9]+(,[0-9]+)*\$`): Search by PubMed ID, e.g. 22472873. Comma separated values accepted up to 20.
- `taxid::IntListParam` (spec: string; pattern `^[0-9]+(,[0-9]+)*\$`): Organism taxon ID. Comma separated values accepted up to 20.
- `dbtype::AbstractString` (spec: string): Cross reference database type, e.g, dbSNP, cosmic curate or ClinVar. Comma separated values accepted up to 2.
- `dbid::AbstractString` (spec: string): Cross-reference database ID, e.g. rs121918508 for dbSNP, COSM29836 for cosmic curated, rcv61200 for ClinVar. Comma separated values accepted up to 20.

# Response
Formats listed in the spec: `application/json`, `application/xml`, `text/x-gff`, `text/x-peff`.
JSON schema: `Vector{ProteinFeatureInfo}`.
Searches can be iterated page by page with `paginate`.
Without `accept` or a `parse` type, `:json` is requested.
